# Verible SystemVerilog style-lint ruleset for claude_verilog_test
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Complements (does NOT replace) the Verilator `make lint` semantic check.
# Verible enforces *style consistency*; Verilator catches semantic/structural
# bugs (widths, latches, unused signals).
#
# Curated to match the existing RTL house style: 4-space indent, lower
# snake_case signals with _q (registered) / _w (combinational) suffixes,
# ALL_CAPS parameters, packed enums/structs, files named after their module.
#
# Syntax (one directive per line):
#   +rule              enable a rule
#   -rule              disable a rule
#   rule=param:value   configure a rule
# Default rule set + full reference:
#   https://chipsalliance.github.io/verible/lint.html
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Disabled: pure house-style conflicts (would be noise, not findings) -----

# Long lines are pervasive and intentional — hand-aligned AXI port maps and
# descriptive block comments. (median file has a ~110-col line; p90 ~200.)
-line-length

# Parameters / localparams use ALL_CAPS (e.g. AXI_ADDR_WIDTH, N_MASTERS),
# not Verible's default CamelCase expectation. Re-enable as a configured
# ALL_CAPS check once the rest of the ruleset is clean.
-parameter-name-style

# Parameters are declared without an explicit storage type by convention
# (e.g. `parameter DEPTH = 8`). Enabling this flags ~80 sites — pure house
# style, not a defect. Revisit if the team adopts typed parameters.
-explicit-parameter-storage-type

# Memory/array unpacked dimensions are written `[0:DEPTH-1]` deliberately for
# readability; Verible prefers `[DEPTH]`. ~40 sites — stylistic preference.
-unpacked-dimensions-range-ordering

# --- Configured (bead hn9l) --------------------------------------------------

# Several `always_ff` blocks declare block-local temporaries (`logic do_fire;`,
# `logic [31:0] csr_cur, csr_nxt;`, `automatic real vt, cpr, ...`) and assign
# them with blocking `=`. That is legal and idiomatic (combinational scratch
# values inside a clocked block), but the rule's default (waive_for_locals =
# false) flags every blocking assignment in an always_ff, locals included:
# 38 findings, 34 in rv32i_csr_file.sv and 4 in pll_rnm.sv. Each of the 38 was
# checked by hand against its declaration: all are block-local variables.
# `waive_for_locals` exempts exactly that case, so a blocking assignment to a
# module-level signal (the real hazard this rule exists for) is STILL an
# error. This is deliberately a rule parameter rather than a --waiver_files
# entry or inline pragma, which would suppress the rule on those lines
# whatever is assigned. Negative-controlled in bead hn9l.
always-ff-non-blocking=waive_for_locals:true

# --- Kept at default (report as warnings; high-value structural/style) -------
# Notably still enabled and meaningful on this codebase:
#   case-missing-default      — guards against unintended latches/incomplete cases
#   always-ff-non-blocking    — sequential-logic blocking-assignment discipline
#   no-trailing-spaces, no-tabs, enum-name-style, module-filename,
#   packed-dimensions-range-ordering, explicit-function-lifetime, generate-label.
# The whole tree is clean against this ruleset (bead hn9l) and the CI lint step
# is a hard gate: any new finding fails the build.
